00:32:25.100 --> 00:32:29.200
<v Marcus Webb>Noted. Add BPAY to the release two list if we're not doing third-party transfers in MVP.</v>

110
00:32:29.200 --> 00:32:31.600
<v James Park>Actually BPAY might be possible in MVP — it's a well-understood integration with existing infrastructure. Let me check our current core banking capabilities and come back on that.</v>

111
00:32:31.600 --> 00:32:34.800
<v Marcus Webb>Perfect. Rachel — anything on the navigation architecture from a technical standpoint?</v>

112
00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:58.400
<v Rachel Torres>The tab navigation itself is straightforward. What I'd flag is deep linking — the ability for a notification or external link to bring the customer directly to a specific screen within the app. For example, if Nova sends a notification about a transaction, tapping it should take you directly to that transaction in the account detail screen, not just to the home screen. Deep linking is something we should design for from the start even if we don't have the notifications feature yet. It affects how we structure our navigation routing in the app.</v>

113
00:32:58.400 --> 00:33:02.800
<v James Park>Agreed. We'll implement React Navigation or equivalent with a deep link handler from day one. Low cost to add, high cost to retrofit.</v>

114
00:33:02.800 --> 00:33:22.800
<v Marcus Webb>Excellent. I think we've covered a remarkable amount of ground. Let me do a final summary before we close. What are our main takeaways and actions?</v>

115
