<v Marcus Webb>First, MVP scope is confirmed as: home screen with account cards and balance visibility toggle, account detail with ninety-day transaction history and date filter, own-account transfer, on-screen statement view, CSV export, Nova chatbot with five read-only intents, and foundational architecture including security and feature flags. The offset account shows balance and linked badge with a static explanation, no live mortgage data in MVP. Second — design refinements to action before next review: Sarah to update the account card to mask account numbers by default, reconsider the three-button layout to give Transfer prominence, add a cached balance indicator for offline states, and review all labels for jargon. Third — architecture tasks: Rachel to document the proposed auth flow including session management and biometric design intent. Rachel to document the caching strategy. Fourth — team resourcing: add a content designer to the project team. Fifth — things deferred to release two and beyond: PDF statements, third-party transfers, push notifications, interest savings on offset, full filter, dark mode, spending categories. And deferred long-term: financial advice features, Nova transactional capability, open banking, real-time notifications infrastructure.</v>

